# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: native-pipeline-yaml-not-linted -- an invalid rule in .gitlab/native.yml passes every repo check and silently kills the child pipeline
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: ci-infra
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-native-pipeline-yaml-lint
#+DATE: 2026-10-08

* Symptom

MR !462 (IntersectWith) added four probe jobs to =.gitlab/native.yml= with
=if: '$$MACOS_RUNNER == "online" && ...'= (a doubled =$=). GitLab rejects that
expression ("rule if invalid expression syntax"), so the parent's
=native:pipeline= bridge failed with =downstream_pipeline_creation_failed=
twice (pipelines 2925982648, 2926066881) and NO macOS / Windows job of that MR
ran -- not only the new probes, every native lane. The bridge's failure
reason says nothing about the YAML; the cause was only found by posting the
file to the project's CI lint API (=ci/lint= with the file as =content=):

#+begin_example
valid: False
ERROR jobs:intersectwith:probe:bricscad:macos:rules:rule if invalid expression syntax
...
#+end_example

=check-native-pipeline-changes=, =check-probe-families=,
=check-cad-sweep-gating= and =glab ci lint= (which lints =.gitlab-ci.yml=,
not the included child file) all passed.

* Fix

Lint =.gitlab/native.yml= itself in the repo checks: a script posting it to
the CI lint endpoint (needs a token -- fine in CI, optional locally), or an
offline check for the shapes GitLab rejects (a =$$NAME= in a =rules: if=,
unbalanced quotes / regex slashes). Run it in =check-native-pipeline-changes=
or as its own make target in the lint lane.

Fixed by hand in MR !462 (commit 89a9921e).

* Fix (2026-10-22)

=scripts/check-native-pipeline-yaml.py= -- an OFFLINE check (PyYAML, no
token, no network) of =.gitlab/native.yml= for the shapes GitLab refuses:

- every =rules:= (jobs and =workflow:=): not a list, an entry that is not a
  mapping, an unknown rule key, an unknown =when:=, an =if:= that is not a
  string;
- every =if:= run through a small lexer + parser of GitLab's expression
  grammar (=$NAME=, '..' / ".." strings, =/regex/flags=, =null=, ~==~ ~!=~
  ~=~~ ~!~~ ~&&~ ~||~ =( )=): a =$= not followed by a name (=$$NAME=, the
  !462 case), unterminated quotes, an unterminated regex, a bad flag, a
  regex Python cannot compile, a match against a non-regex, unbalanced
  parentheses, a dangling =&&= / =||=, two operands with no operator;
- =extends:= to an unknown job or in a cycle; a visible job with no
  =script:= / =trigger:= / =run:= once its =extends:= chain is merged
  (hidden =.templates= exempt); a =needs:= naming a job not in the file
  (unless =optional:=, =pipeline:= or =project:=).

With =GITLAB_TOKEN= set it additionally posts the file to the project's
=ci/lint= API (a network failure there only warns; the offline verdict
stands).

Wired as =make check-native-pipeline-yaml= (Makefile, next to
=check-probe-families=), run by the =documentation= job of =.gitlab-ci.yml=
right after =make check-probe-families= -- the same always-running lint
lane. =python3-yaml= is added to =clautolisp/docker/Dockerfile=, with a
before_script fallback for a stale =:latest=.

Tests: =scripts/tests/test-check-native-pipeline-yaml.py= (32 unittest
cases, run by the make target): each rejected expression shape, a correct
fixture passes, a =$$= rule and an unbalanced quote are caught, the real
=native.yml= passes and a copy with its first =if: '$MACOS_RUNNER= doubled
to =$$= fails. Red/green by hand: the real file -> "OK", exit 0; a copy with
line 700's =$MACOS_RUNNER= doubled -> "encoding:experiment:bricscad:macos:
rules[0]: if: ...: `$' not followed by a variable name at column 1", exit 1;
a copy with that rule's closing =/= dropped -> "unterminated /regex/", exit
1. The parent =.gitlab-ci.yml= also passes it (a sanity check that the
grammar is not stricter than GitLab's).
